WEBVTT

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.620
Opportunity cost is the value of what is not done when time is spent somewhere else.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.340
It is easy to see the meeting, task, favor, or request that receives a yes.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.980
It is harder to see the quiet no that happens at the same time.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.880
Saying yes to a low-value commitment may mean saying no to focused work, maintenance,

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.030
learning, recovery, family time, or a long-term goal that never becomes urgent.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:23.235
Some commitments are visible: meetings on the calendar, project deadlines, school events,

00:00:23.235 --> 00:00:25.380
operational handoffs, and promised deliverables.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.500
Others are hidden: preparation, context switching, travel, cleanup, emotional labor,

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.345
coordination, and the recovery needed after intense work.

00:00:32.345 --> 00:00:34.920
Hidden commitments are where fantasy planning takes root.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.909
A plan looks reasonable because only the obvious work was counted.

00:00:37.909 --> 00:00:39.280
Tradeoffs are not failures.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.230
They are the normal shape of limited capacity.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:43.535
The problem comes when tradeoffs are accidental.

00:00:43.535 --> 00:00:45.330
Urgent work can crowd out important work.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.795
Maintenance can be deferred until it becomes a crisis.

00:00:47.795 --> 00:00:50.540
Learning can be postponed because no one is asking for it today.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:53.120
Relationships and recovery can be treated as flexible,

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.675
even though neglecting them has real consequences.

00:00:55.675 --> 00:00:59.790
Deliberate choice means naming the cost before the calendar spends the time automatically.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.265
Before accepting a request, ask what it displaces.

00:01:02.265 --> 00:01:05.465
Before committing to a goal, ask what support and protection it needs.

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:09.980
Before adding more, ask what should be reduced, paused, delegated, or made simpler.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:14.080
Opportunity cost does not make choices easy, but it makes the real decision visible.
